  "name": "Elder Wand's Wand attacks stack the Artificer's Wand damage debuff (#536)",
  "contract": "Elder Wand 560129 applies aura 42 (proc trigger spell) on Elder Wand 560128, a target debuff whose single effect is SPELL_AURA_MOD_DAMAGE_FROM_CASTER with EffectBasePoints 2 / DieSides 1 (+3%), StackAmount 10 and EffectSpellClassMask word2 0x200, which matches Artificer's Wand 561064's own SpellFamilyFlags [0, 0, 512] and no other family 28 record. Spell.dbc gives 560129's record ProcFlags 0 and no spell_proc row existed, so LoadSpellProcs skipped it and the debuff could never be applied. With a spell_proc row gated on the ranged class damage of Wand of Time and Artificer's Wand - the same definition of \"Wand attacks\" already shipped for Erode Armaments 520386 - each Artificer's Wand hit rolls the record's own 30% ProcChance, which this scenario keeps unchanged. Twenty independent hits are cast because 0.70^20 = 7.98e-4, a false failure below 0.1%; 561064 has RecoveryTime 0 and StartRecoveryTime 0, so the twenty casts are independent and need no cooldown wait. The debuff's DurationIndex 8 is 15000 ms, longer than the 4 s casting window plus the assertion's poll, so a proc on the first hit is still present at the end.",
